Licence
-------
The Z-Anatomy models (and, upstream, BodyParts3D) are licensed
CC BY-SA 4.0 (BodyParts3D itself under CC-BY-SA 2.1 Japan). The full CC BY-SA
4.0 legal text is in LICENSE in this directory (copied verbatim from the
pinned clone's own LICENSE file).

ShareAlike means: a derivative WORK made from this geometry must itself be
distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0 (or a listed BY-SA-compatible licence) --
not plain CC BY, not a proprietary licence, and not "all rights reserved".
Editing, retopologising, decimating, re-triangulating, converting units, or
registering the mesh to a different body does not change this: the protected
expression is the shape, and a modified mesh of the same shape is still an
Adapted Material under Section 1(a) of the licence. See README.md for how
this project isolates that obligation to only the files it actually applies
to.

NOT CC BY-SA -- excluded, non-commercial subcomponents
-------------------------------------------------------
The same Resources/Models/License.txt states that a few named subcomponents
of the release carry a DIFFERENT, more restrictive licence than the rest:

    "Cranial Nerves and Foramina - by University of Dundee, CAHID - CC-BY 4.0"
    "Anatomy of the Inner Ear - by University of Dundee School of Medicine -
     CC-BY-NC-SA 4.0"
    "Kidney - by lissiecowley - CC-BY-NC 4.0"

The Cranial Nerves credit is CC BY 4.0 -- compatible, even more permissive
than the rest of the release. The Inner Ear and Kidney credits carry NC
(NonCommercial), which this project's commercial intent cannot satisfy at
any level of adaptation, independent of the owner's CC BY-SA decision below.
scripts/zanatomy/extract_fbx.py flags any extracted object whose name matches
kidney/renal/cochlea/vestibular/inner-ear/labyrinth patterns as
license != "CC-BY-SA-4.0" in data/derived/zanatomy_inventory.json, and
scripts/zanatomy/map_names.py refuses to map any such object to an atlas
entity id regardless of name score. Some of those name patterns
(cochlear/vestibular nerve and nuclei) could belong to either the CC-BY
Cranial Nerves package or the NC Inner Ear package; flagged conservatively
as excluded pending direct clarification from the Z-Anatomy project, since
NC content shipped in a commercial product cannot be cured after the fact.

Owner decision permitting this material into the repository
-------------------------------------------------------------
2026-09-23 (recorded in full in ../../docs/GEOMETRY_SOURCES.md and
../../PROJECT_STATE.md, Q141): the anatomy MODEL layer (geometry, plus this
project's own corrections to it) may be CC BY-SA compatible. Everything
built on top -- registration to real imaging, ultrasound guidance, needling,
clinical tooling -- stays under the owner's private licence and must live in
separate files that reference the anatomy layer rather than sit inside it.
This replaces the prior blanket rule "no CC BY-SA source may enter it".
